/**
 * @defgroup MCC_Pitch Pitch
 * @ingroup MCC
 * @brief Written pitch primitives: letters, accidentals, note names and
 * pitches.
 *
 * `MCC::Letter` + `MCC::Accidental` form a `MCC::NoteName`, which keeps
 * its written spelling, and a note name plus an octave forms a
 * `MCC::Pitch` (middle C is `C4`). `MCC::PitchClass` and
 * `MCC::ChromaticIndex` discard the spelling and are obtained explicitly.
 * Written equality and order are separate from enharmonic equivalence and
 * pitch height; see @ref MCC_Specification.
 *
 * All types are trivially copyable, allocation-free and `constexpr`.
 * Available when `MCC_PITCH` is defined.
 */
